<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Themis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Themis was the Greek goddess of divine law, order and custom, a Titan and daughter of Gaia and Uranus. By <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> she was mother of the Horai and, in some accounts, the Fates. Greek tradition held that she possessed the oracle of Delphi before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a>, and she was often shown holding scales as a figure of justice.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/themis.jpg" alt="Themis" width="320" height="598" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo André Frantz (Tetraktys) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0029MAN-Themis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
